  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "$A$ whistle whose air column is open at both ends has a fundamental frequency of $5100 \\mathrm{Hz}$. If the speed of sound in air is $340 \\mathrm{ms}^{-1}$, the length of the whistle, in $\\mathrm{cm}$, is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "bm72v",
      "text": "$5 / 3$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "dylPC",
      "text": "$10 / 3$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "fkvyL",
      "text": "5",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "keS7g",
      "text": "$20 / 3$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For an open pipe, the frequency\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\nf=\\frac{v}{2 l} \\Rightarrow 5100=\\frac{340}{2 \\times 1} \\\\\r\nl=\\frac{340}{5100 \\times 2} \\Rightarrow l=\\frac{2}{30 \\times 2}=\\frac{1}{30} \\mathrm{m} \\\\\r\nl=\\frac{100}{30}=\\frac{10}{3} \\mathrm{cm}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
